WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:12.690
The most important issue facing the British
electorate is their own self-government.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.490
Under the European Union, more and more power
has flowed to Brussels.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:22.500
The British Parliament is less and less important
in setting British domestic policy.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.279
Parliament can’t reverse decisions that
are made in Brussels by bureaucrats and diplomats,

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:33.650
and people all over the European Union have
given this issue the name “democratic deficit.”

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:39.210
I’ve always thought that the economic issues
were secondary for the British, indeed, for

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.010
everybody in the Europe.

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:46.400
Nobody is going to argue with a continent-wide
free trade zone, but honestly, the founders

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.810
of the European Union had something very different
in mind.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:54.940
It’s fundamental to the European Union itself
that the people shouldn’t be allowed to

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.800
have too much say over these decisions.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:02.570
So I would say to the Brits: Get out now because
this may be your only chance.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:06.710
If you don’t take it, you’re going to
become a county in a larger Europe.

